.TH KEYHOLDER 1 "October 2026" "Keyholder 0.2.0" "Operator Commands"
.SH NAME
keyholder \- securely administer Keyholder and its configured subscription backend
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keyholder
.RI [ global-options ]
.I resource action
.RI [ action-options ]
.br
.B keyholder help
.RI [ resource " " action ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B keyholder
is the supported operator interface for Keyholder. By default it sends a small JSON
request through an SSH alias to the root-owned host dispatcher. Administrator API
credentials remain on the server. Secret subscription and panel URLs are printed only
to an interactive terminal or written to a newly created mode-0600 file.
.PP
Marzban is the default upstream backend. Customer identity, stable public subscription
tokens and optional rendering policy belong to Keyholder; quota, expiry, status,
traffic counters, credentials and inbound selection belong to the upstream backend.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-host " " ALIAS
SSH alias for administration. The default is keyholder-server or the configured value.
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " " ID
Backend namespace. The default is marzban-default.
.TP
.B \-\-local
Run the dispatcher locally. This is restricted to root on the VPS and cannot open the panel tunnel.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Return machine-readable JSON for nonsecret results.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the installed version.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B help [RESOURCE [ACTION]]
Show the resource list, one resource's actions, or detailed action help.
.TP
.B config init [--output FILE]
Create a new private environment template. Existing files are never overwritten.
.TP
.BR "system status" ", " "system health" ", " "system doctor"
Inspect containers and revision; check application health; or audit migrations, vault,
mappings, stable links and upstream inventory.
.TP
.B system metrics
Show live RAM, swap, disk, load, uptime and network counters with the latest sampled CPU usage.
.TP
.B system backup
Create a root-only recovery set containing Keyholder data, required secret configuration,
configured ingress files and consistent SQLite snapshots.
.TP
.BR "backend list" ", " "backend register"
List backend registrations or register the backend supplied by deployment configuration.
.TP
.BR "upstream users" ", " "upstream inbounds"
List upstream users or available inbound tags without returning credentials.
.TP
.B upstream sync
Create missing Keyholder registrations for active upstream users. Existing canonical
registrations and URLs are preserved.
.TP
.B upstream reconcile --confirm
Repair legacy duplicate registrations. This is a recovery operation and can rotate links.
.TP
.B user create USERNAME --quota-gb GB --days DAYS --protocols PROTOCOL... [identity options] [--save-link FILE]
Create a Marzban user and its canonical Keyholder registration. A zero quota means
unlimited; zero days means no expiry. Identity options are --name, --telegram and --phone.
.TP
.B user attach USERNAME [--name NAME] [--telegram ID] [--phone NUMBER] [--profiles KIND...] [--save-link FILE]
Attach an existing active upstream user. The operation is idempotent and returns the
same canonical URL when the mapping already exists.
.TP
.B user update USERNAME [--quota-gb GB] [--days DAYS] [--status active|disabled]
Change upstream plan fields. Expiry is calculated from the time of the update and traffic
is not reset.
.TP
.B user inbounds USERNAME --protocol PROTOCOL --tags [TAG...]
Replace only one protocol's upstream inbound selection. An empty tag list disables that
protocol while preserving credentials and other selections.
.TP
.BR "user usage USERNAME" ", " "user reset-usage USERNAME --confirm"
Read plan and traffic state, or explicitly reset used traffic.
.TP
.B customer list [--limit N] [--offset N] [--history]
List canonical customers without bearer tokens. History includes revoked registrations.
.TP
.B customer update SELECTOR [--name NAME] [--telegram ID|--clear-telegram] [--phone NUMBER|--clear-phone]
Update private Keyholder identity fields. Phone and Telegram values are nullable and unique.
.TP
.BR "customer show SELECTOR" ", " "customer check SELECTOR"
Show a customer mapping, or validate its upstream profiles and rendered subscription.
.TP
.B customer link SELECTOR [--info] [--save-link FILE]
Retrieve the existing stable subscription URL. The info option selects the human-readable
usage URL without changing the customer token.
.TP
.BR "customer enable SELECTOR" ", " "customer disable SELECTOR"
Resume or pause Keyholder subscription delivery. This does not disable already imported
upstream credentials.
.TP
.B customer rename SELECTOR NAME
Change Keyholder's private display name without changing the upstream username.
.TP
.B customer remap SELECTOR USERNAME
Map the same customer and stable URL to a replacement upstream username.
.TP
.B customer profiles SELECTOR KIND...
Set a customer rendering override. Omit overrides in normal Marzban-authoritative operation.
.TP
.B customer revoke SELECTOR --confirm
Permanently revoke the Keyholder registration.
.TP
.B customer rotate-token SELECTOR --confirm [--save-link FILE]
Replace the bearer token. The previous subscription URL immediately stops working.
.TP
.B panel open [--port PORT] [--no-browser]
Open an SSH tunnel from 127.0.0.1:PORT to the loopback-only Marzban panel. Keep the
terminal open while using the panel.
.TP
.B panel url [--save-link FILE]
Read the prepared legacy private bookmark. The SSH tunnel is the preferred panel path.
.TP
.BR "monitor status" ", " "monitor run"
Read the last monitor result or run checks immediately without sending notifications.
.TP
.B monitor controls
List notification rules, active incidents, acknowledgements and silences.
.TP
.B monitor ack KEY | monitor unack KEY
Acknowledge or unacknowledge the current alert occurrence and threshold.
.TP
.B monitor silence KEY [--hours HOURS] | monitor unsilence KEY
Temporarily mute one exact alert key, for at most 168 hours (default 24).
.TP
.B monitor rule-disable RULE --confirm | monitor rule-enable RULE
Disable or enable notifications for one rule. Checks and health remain active.
.TP
.BR "alert-bot configure" ", " "alert-bot status" ", " "alert-bot test"
Interactively configure, inspect and test the dedicated Telegram alert bot.
.TP
.BR "heartbeat configure" ", " "heartbeat test"
Interactively configure and test an external Better Stack heartbeat for total-host outages.
.TP
.BR "management-bot configure" ", " "management-bot status" ", " "management-bot test"
Configure the allowlisted Telegram management bot, inspect its unit state, or send a test.
The management bot never returns subscription links.
.SH SELECTORS
Customer operations accept a customer UUID, exact upstream username, Telegram handle or
numeric ID, or phone number. Use the UUID when a human identifier could be ambiguous.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B $KEYHOLDER_ADMIN_CONFIG
Optional workstation JSON configuration. A checkout defaults to .private/admin.json.
.TP
.B /usr/local/lib/keyholder-admin/host.py
Default root-owned server dispatcher.
.TP
.B /etc/keyholder/monitor.env
Root-only alert and heartbeat secrets.
.TP
.B /etc/keyholder/management-bot.env
Root-only management bot token and administrator ID.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means success. One means an operation or health check failed. Two is used by the
monitor for execution/configuration failure. Interrupted panel tunnels return 130.
.SH SECURITY
Subscription URLs are bearer credentials. Prefer --save-link to a private file and never
place them in logs, shell history, chat, tickets or monitoring URLs. Bot tokens are entered
interactively without terminal echo. Destructive and link-breaking commands require --confirm.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
keyholder system doctor
keyholder user create customer_001 --name "Alice Example" \
  --quota-gb 20 --days 30 --protocols vless trojan
keyholder customer link customer_001 --save-link ./customer_001.json
keyholder customer update customer_001 --telegram @alice --clear-phone
keyholder panel open
keyholder help user inbounds
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR ufw (8)
